From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lech Piekarski <isilweo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:38:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: drop the low VFE clock levels on MSM8953

For RDI the computed VFE rate is about 45 MHz, which cannot keep up with
the memory writes on MSM8953 and drops lines. The vendor software runs the
VFE at 266.67 MHz. Start the MSM8953 (and SDM450) VFE clock table at that
level.

Tested on MSM8953 with an S5KC505A at 1304x980 RDI: the VFE runs at
266.67 MHz and libcamera captures at 30.4 fps without sequence gaps.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Source: https://github.com/isilweo/linux/commit/67c43fe73975320a4f827f80b8aa7b2db2c80e6b
Base-commit: 1c1a919fd728c881e7ccaf3cf18a3cf3055e0429
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 10 ++++------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
index 85837e579210..9cbff8c7b95e 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -452,9 +452,8 @@ static const struct camss_subdev_resources vfe_res_8x53[] = {
 		.clock_rate = { { 0 },
 				{ 0 },
 				{ 0 },
-				{ 50000000, 100000000, 133330000,
-				  160000000, 200000000, 266670000,
-				  310000000, 400000000, 465000000 },
+				{ 266670000, 310000000, 400000000,
+				  465000000 },
 				{ 0 },
 				{ 0 },
 				{ 0 } },
@@ -481,9 +480,8 @@ static const struct camss_subdev_resources vfe_res_8x53[] = {
 		.clock_rate = { { 0 },
 				{ 0 },
 				{ 0 },
-				{ 50000000, 100000000, 133330000,
-				  160000000, 200000000, 266670000,
-				  310000000, 400000000, 465000000 },
+				{ 266670000, 310000000, 400000000,
+				  465000000 },
 				{ 0 },
 				{ 0 },
 				{ 0 } },
